{"id":"bang-patrol-3","title":"BANG's third war patrol: three convoy attacks","short":"Patrol 3 · September 1944","eyebrow":"South of Honshu and east of Formosa · BANG's third war patrol","lede":"BANG's six torpedo attacks of September 1944, as typed on her attack sheets, with her depth log and the Japanese record where one has been found. Times are converted to GMT, with Tokyo time alongside.","places":[{"name":"Philippine Sea","lon":137.3,"lat":28.45},{"name":"Formosa","lon":121.6,"lat":24.4,"inset":[120.6,23.0]},{"name":"Yonaguni","lon":123.0,"lat":24.38,"small":true},{"name":"Iriomote","lon":123.82,"lat":24.2,"small":true},{"name":"Ishigaki","lon":124.17,"lat":24.3,"small":true},{"name":"Miyako","lon":125.3,"lat":24.6,"small":true},{"name":"Honshu","lon":138.3,"lat":35.6,"inset":[138.3,36.2]}],"notes":[{"head":"Reading the map.","text":"Positions are BANG's own dead reckoning and star sights; lines between them are straight, and where she went in between is not recorded. Open circles are ships she sighted, at the target's position. As the clock passes each firing time a red ring pulses at BANG's position; hover a diamond for the attack sheet."},{"head":"Clocks.","text":"BANG kept zone K (−10) throughout. Japanese records use Tokyo time (I, −9)."},{"head":"Records with no time.","text":"Neither Japanese record for this patrol gives a time: combinedfleet.com's account of convoy No. 3905 and the 4th Surface Escort Division's daily summary for TAKA-909. Each is drawn at the time of the attack it matches, and marked so. FRUPAC's intercept has No. 3905's ships \"torp & sunk 1520/09\" (1520 I = 1620 K, between Attacks 1 and 2)."},{"head":"What is missing.","text":"No Japanese record has been found yet for Attacks 5 and 6 (20–21 September); the 4th Escort diary has no attack on those days. Where the Japanese record names only the ships that were hit, the rest of the convoy is described as BANG saw it."},{"head":"Sources.","text":"BANG's third war patrol report, NARA microfilm M1752 (74802831). The 4th Surface Escort Division / Okinawa Base Force war diary, September 1944, via JACAR (C08030144100, National Institute for Defense Studies). Convoy No. 3905 from combinedfleet.com, a secondary source, flagged where used. Coastline: Natural Earth."}],"boats":[{"id":"bang","name":"BANG","hull":"SS-385","co":"LCdr A. R. Gallaher","patrol_no":3}],"others":[],"actions":[{"id":"no3905","label":"9 September 1944","convoy":"No. 3905","start":"1944-09-09T01:00Z","end":"1944-09-09T12:00Z","route":"Yokosuka → Haha-jima.","ships_note":"Ships and escorts from combinedfleet.com. BANG saw 1 AO, 2 AK and 2 escorts.","outcome":"Tokiwasan Maru (1,804 tons) and Shoryu Maru (1,916 tons) sunk at 28-58N 137-45E (combinedfleet.com; no primary record found yet). BANG claimed a medium AK and a medium AO.","ships":[{"name":"Tokiwasan Maru","kind":"Merchant","type":"cargo","sunk":true},{"name":"Shoryu Maru","kind":"Merchant","type":"cargo","sunk":true}],"escorts":[{"name":"Yasojima","kind":"Escort","type":"escort","sunk":false},{"name":"Hachijo","kind":"Kaibokan","type":"escort","sunk":false},{"name":"CD-4","kind":"Kaibokan","type":"escort","sunk":false},{"name":"CD-12","kind":"Kaibokan","type":"escort","sunk":false}],"sil_note":"Silhouettes show the kind of ship (fleet submarine, destroyer, escort, auxiliary gunboat, merchant ship, tanker, fighter aircraft), not each one's own outline, and are not to scale.","box":[137.267,28.583,138.1,29.317],"tracks":{"bang":[{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-09-01T21:00Z","lat":28.2,"lon":-177.3833,"kind":"narrative","ref":"depart Midway","on_track":true,"local":"1944-09-01 0900 (Y)","raw":"28-12N 177-23W","note":"Departed Midway enroute area. Crossed date line (port position)","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p03","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0048.jpg"},{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-09-09T06:16Z","lat":28.8833,"lon":137.7,"kind":"attack","ref":"Attack 1","on_track":true,"local":"1944-09-09 1616 (K)","raw":"28-53N 137-42E","note":"Torpedo attack No. 1","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p13","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0058.jpg"},{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-09-09T06:32Z","lat":28.9167,"lon":137.7,"kind":"attack","ref":"Attack 2","on_track":true,"local":"1944-09-09 1632 (K)","raw":"28-55N 137-42E","note":"Torpedo attack No. 2 (time 1616-32)","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p15","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0060.jpg"},{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-09-09T19:50Z","lat":29.0667,"lon":137.5833,"kind":"bt","ref":"BT","on_track":true,"local":"1944-09-09 1950 (Z)","raw":"29-04N 137-35E","note":"","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p28","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0073.jpg"}]},"fixes":[{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-09-09T03:05Z","lat":29.0167,"lon":137.6167,"kind":"ship","ref":"Ship 1","on_track":false,"local":"1944-09-09 1305 (K)","raw":"29-01N 137-37E","note":"Convoy (1 AO 2 AK 2 escorts) 32000 yds; attacks 1 & 2","fix":"ship-contact positions are the target not BANG","page":"rg367-74802831/p10","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0055.jpg"},{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-09-09T06:16Z","lat":28.8833,"lon":137.7,"kind":"attack","ref":"Attack 1","on_track":true,"local":"1944-09-09 1616 (K)","raw":"28-53N 137-42E","note":"Torpedo attack No. 1","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p13","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0058.jpg"},{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-09-09T06:32Z","lat":28.9167,"lon":137.7,"kind":"attack","ref":"Attack 2","on_track":true,"local":"1944-09-09 1632 (K)","raw":"28-55N 137-42E","note":"Torpedo attack No. 2 (time 1616-32)","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p15","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0060.jpg"}],"events":[{"utc":"1944-09-09T03:05Z","side":"bang","type":"contact","title":"Ship contact (1)","text":"Convoy (1 AO 2 AK 2 escorts) 32000 yds; attacks 1 & 2","local":"1944-09-09 1305 (K)","doubt":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p10","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0055.jpg"},{"utc":"1944-09-09T06:16Z","side":"bang","type":"attack","title":"Attack 1","text":"Torpedo attack No. 1","outcome":"Tokiwasan Maru (1,804 t) and Shoryu Maru (1,916 t) of convoy No. 3905, Yokosuka to Haha-jima, both sunk. BANG claimed a medium AK and a medium AO (Attacks 1-2, 1616-1632 K). Secondary source only.","local":"1944-09-09 1616 (K)","doubt":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p13","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0058.jpg","lat":28.8833,"lon":137.7},{"utc":"1944-09-09T06:16Z","side":"japan","type":"sank","title":"Tokiwasan Maru and Shoryu Maru","text":"Convoy No. 3905 (Yokosuka to Haha-jima; escorts Yasojima, Hachijo, CD-4, CD-12): BANG torpedoes and sinks both Tokiwasan Maru and Shoryu Maru at 28-58N 137-45E","original":"","local":"1944-09-09 no time (I, Tokyo)","page":"combinedfleet:yasojima_t","scan":"https://www.combinedfleet.com/yasojima_t.htm","doubt":"Secondary source (combinedfleet.com). The record gives no time; drawn at the time of the attack it matches (Attack 1).","ship_type":"cargo","lat":28.9667,"lon":137.75},{"utc":"1944-09-09T06:17Z","side":"bang","type":"dive","title":"Ordered 400 ft","text":"I swung around and saw that the leading escort was heading toward me - ordered 400 feet.","local":"1944-09-09 1617 (K)","page":"rg367-74802831/p04","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0049.jpg"},{"utc":"1944-09-09T06:19Z","side":"bang","type":"dive","title":"Passing 350 ft","text":"Received the first pattern of depth charges while passing 350 feet all above.","local":"1944-09-09 1619 (K)","page":"rg367-74802831/p04","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0049.jpg"},{"utc":"1944-09-09T06:21Z","side":"bang","type":"dive","title":"Ordered 450 ft (70)","text":"Running at 450 feet at 2/3 speed under a 17° negative gradient. ... During the next hour and a half they dropped about 70 depth charges many of them very close.","local":"1944-09-09 1621 (K)","page":"rg367-74802831/p04","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0049.jpg"},{"utc":"1944-09-09T06:32Z","side":"bang","type":"attack","title":"Attack 2","text":"Torpedo attack No. 2 (time 1616-32)","outcome":"","local":"1944-09-09 1632 (K)","doubt":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p15","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0060.jpg","lat":28.9167,"lon":137.7},{"utc":"1944-09-09T08:10Z","side":"bang","type":"dive","title":"Ordered 475 ft (16)","text":"16 depth charges about one second apart above very slightly and to port very slightly. We were at 475 feet when they started (time approximate: ~1h50m after firing)","local":"1944-09-09 1810 (K)","page":"rg367-74802831/p05","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0050.jpg"},{"utc":"1944-09-09T08:11Z","side":"bang","type":"dive","title":"Ordered 580 ft (1)","text":"but the bow was knocked down and we were at 580 feet making standard speed with a 10 degree up angle before we caught the boat. ... I heard a definite thump on the hull followed by a tremendous explosion. I believe this was a depth charge that bounced off our side.","local":"1944-09-09 1811 (K)","page":"rg367-74802831/p05","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0050.jpg"}],"sinkings":[{"utc":"1944-09-09T06:16Z","side":"japan","type":"sank","title":"Tokiwasan Maru and Shoryu Maru","text":"Convoy No. 3905 (Yokosuka to Haha-jima; escorts Yasojima, Hachijo, CD-4, CD-12): BANG torpedoes and sinks both Tokiwasan Maru and Shoryu Maru at 28-58N 137-45E","original":"","local":"1944-09-09 no time (I, Tokyo)","page":"combinedfleet:yasojima_t","scan":"https://www.combinedfleet.com/yasojima_t.htm","doubt":"Secondary source (combinedfleet.com). The record gives no time; drawn at the time of the attack it matches (Attack 1).","ship_type":"cargo","lat":28.9667,"lon":137.75}],"estimates":[],"land":[]},{"id":"taka-909","label":"19 September 1944","convoy":"TAKA-909","start":"1944-09-18T18:00Z","end":"1944-09-19T05:00Z","route":"Takao → Kagoshima.","ships_note":"Escorts from the 4th Surface Escort Division's war diary, which names only the ship sunk. BANG saw 8 merchantmen including an AO, and 5 or more escorts.","outcome":"No. 2 Tosei Maru sunk. BANG claimed one AK sunk and another probably sunk. CD-30 and Taian Maru, with army aircraft, attacked her and claimed \"one enemy submarine sunk\"; BANG surfaced that night after about 80 depth charges.","ships":[{"name":"No. 2 Tosei Maru","kind":"Tanker, 507 tons","type":"tanker","sunk":true}],"escorts":[{"name":"CD-30","kind":"Kaibokan","type":"escort","sunk":false},{"name":"W-15","kind":"Minesweeper","type":"escort","sunk":false},{"name":"No. 3 Takunan Maru","kind":"Auxiliary escort","type":"gunboat","sunk":false},{"name":"Shichiri Maru","kind":"Auxiliary escort","type":"gunboat","sunk":false},{"name":"Taian Maru","kind":"Auxiliary escort","type":"gunboat","sunk":false},{"name":"No. 3 Taihei Maru","kind":"Auxiliary escort","type":"gunboat","sunk":false}],"sil_note":"Silhouettes show the kind of ship (fleet submarine, destroyer, escort, auxiliary gunboat, merchant ship, tanker, fighter aircraft), not each one's own outline, and are not to scale.","box":[121.892,24.6,122.733,25.283],"tracks":{"bang":[{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-09-17T20:40Z","lat":25.0,"lon":123.5,"kind":"bt","ref":"BT","on_track":true,"local":"1944-09-17 2040 (Z)","raw":"25-00N 123-30E","note":"","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p28","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0073.jpg"},{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-09-18T23:15Z","lat":24.9333,"lon":122.2417,"kind":"attack","ref":"Attack 3","on_track":true,"local":"1944-09-19 0915 (K)","raw":"24-56N 122-14.5E","note":"Torpedo attack No. 3","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p17","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0062.jpg"},{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-09-18T23:55Z","lat":24.9333,"lon":122.2417,"kind":"attack","ref":"Attack 4","on_track":true,"local":"1944-09-19 0955 (K)","raw":"24-56N 122-14.5E","note":"Torpedo attack No. 4 (time 0915-55)","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p19","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0064.jpg"},{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-09-19T20:51Z","lat":24.0,"lon":122.0,"kind":"bt","ref":"BT","on_track":true,"local":"1944-09-19 2051 (Z)","raw":"24-00N 122-00E","note":"","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p28","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0073.jpg"}]},"fixes":[{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-09-18T20:15Z","lat":24.9833,"lon":122.35,"kind":"ship","ref":"Ship 2","on_track":false,"local":"1944-09-19 0615 (K)","raw":"24-59N 122-21E","note":"Convoy (8 merchantmen incl. AO; 5+ escorts) 30000 yds; attacks 3 & 4","fix":"ship-contact positions are the target not BANG","page":"rg367-74802831/p10","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0055.jpg"},{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-09-18T23:15Z","lat":24.9333,"lon":122.2417,"kind":"attack","ref":"Attack 3","on_track":true,"local":"1944-09-19 0915 (K)","raw":"24-56N 122-14.5E","note":"Torpedo attack No. 3","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p17","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0062.jpg"},{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-09-18T23:55Z","lat":24.9333,"lon":122.2417,"kind":"attack","ref":"Attack 4","on_track":true,"local":"1944-09-19 0955 (K)","raw":"24-56N 122-14.5E","note":"Torpedo attack No. 4 (time 0915-55)","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p19","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0064.jpg"}],"events":[{"utc":"1944-09-18T20:15Z","side":"bang","type":"contact","title":"Ship contact (2)","text":"Convoy (8 merchantmen incl. AO; 5+ escorts) 30000 yds; attacks 3 & 4","local":"1944-09-19 0615 (K)","doubt":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p10","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0055.jpg"},{"utc":"1944-09-18T20:51Z","side":"bang","type":"dive","title":"Ordered 350 ft","text":"Submerged to 350 feet to get bathythermograph indication","local":"1944-09-19 0651 (K)","page":"rg367-74802831/p06","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0051.jpg"},{"utc":"1944-09-18T23:15Z","side":"bang","type":"attack","title":"Attack 3","text":"Torpedo attack No. 3","outcome":"No. 2 Tosei Maru (507-ton tanker) of convoy TAKA-909 sunk. BANG claimed one AK sunk and another probably sunk (Attacks 3-4); the escorts claimed BANG sunk.","local":"1944-09-19 0915 (K)","doubt":"","page":"rg367-74802831/p17","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0062.jpg","lat":24.9333,"lon":122.2417},{"utc":"1944-09-18T23:15Z","side":"japan","type":"sank","title":"Tosei Maru No. 2","text":"CD-30, W-15, No. 3 Takunan Maru, Shichiri Maru, Taian Maru, No. 3 Taihei Maru: escorting convoy TAKA-909. / CD-30 and Taian Maru, with army aircraft, attack the enemy submarine that torpedoed convoy TAKA-909 at N 24°54′ E 122°23′. / Damage: No. 2 Tosei Maru sunk. Result: one enemy submarine sunk","original":"海防三〇、掃一五、三拓南丸、七利丸、太安丸、三号太平丸 タカ九〇九船団護衛 / 海防三〇、太安丸陸軍飛行機ト共ニN二四─五四 E一二二─二三ニ於テタカ九〇九船団ヲ雷撃セル敵潜水艦攻撃 / 被害 第二東勢丸沈没 戦果 敵潜水艦一隻撃沈","local":"1944-09-19 no time (I, Tokyo)","page":"jacar:C08030144100 p12","scan":"https://www.jacar.archives.go.jp/das/image/C08030144100","doubt":"The record gives no time; drawn at the time of the attack it matches (Attack 3).","ship_type":"tanker","lat":24.9,"lon":122.3833},{"utc":"1944-09-18T23:16Z","side":"bang","type":"dive","title":"Ordered 400 ft","text":"Went immediately to 400 feet as I had seen another escort ... at about 2000 yards with a 0° angle on the bow.","local":"1944-09-19 0916 (K)","page":"rg367-74802831/p07","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0052.jpg"},{"utc":"1944-09-18T23:20Z","side":"bang","type":"dive","title":"Ordered 450 ft (80)","text":"Very deliberate depth charging began 4 minutes after firing. Three escorts ... let us have about 80 charges in patterns of 3 6 or 9 during the next 4½ hours. We were running silent at 450 feet under a 24 degree negative gradient.","local":"1944-09-19 0920 (K)","page":"rg367-74802831/p07","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US